    "body": "@annevk thanks for the answer. \r\n\r\nI now understand that the \"slot\" attribute of a slotable sets the slotable \"name\". Everywhere else in the document, a slotable's \"name\" refers to what is set in the \"slot\" attribute, so everything is consistent. I was just confused that an attribute named \"slot\" could set something called a \"name\" and assumed this was an error.\r\n\r\nNot sure more examples are needed here. If a slotable's name was referred to as \"slotName\" instead of \"name\", it would have been easier to understand for me but I am not used to read specs. \r\n\r\nClosing this, thanks for taking the time to answer!",
